# Chili Lime Black Bean Tacos

Based on [https://www.washingtonpost.com/recipes/…](https://www.washingtonpost.com/recipes/chili-lime-black-bean-tacos/17008) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20210203164149/https://www.washingtonpost.com/recipes/chili-lime-black-bean-tacos/17008))

{ rating="4" image="chili_lime_black_bean_tacos.jpeg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 4 [scallions]{ ing="scallions" }
- [ ] 1 [red onion]{ ing="red-onion" }, thinly sliced
- [ ] 1/2 cup [lime juice]{ ing="lime-juice" } (from 2 or 3 limes)
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [Kosher salt]{ ing="kosher-salt" }
- [ ] ~4 Tbsp [extra-virgin olive oil]{ ing="extra-virgin-olive-oil" }
- [ ] 2x 15.5-ounce can [no-salt-added black beans]{ ing="no-salt-added-black-beans" }, with the liquid
- [ ] 2 tsp [chili powder]{ ing="chili-powder" }
- [ ] 2 tsp [ground cumin]{ ing="ground-cumin" }
- [ ] 2 tsp [Spanish smoked paprika]{ ing="spanish-smoked-paprika" } (pimentón; sweet or hot)
- [ ] 1 tsp [Dijon mustard]{ ing="dijon-mustard" }
- [ ] 12 6[-inch corn tortillas]{ ing="inch-corn-tortillas" }
- [ ] 2 cups [chopped romaine lettuce]{ ing="chopped-romaine-lettuce" } (from 1 heart of romaine)
- [ ] [Hot sauce]{ ing="hot-sauce" }, such as Cholula
- [ ] Other optional [toppings including avocado]{ ing="toppings-including-avocado" }, tomato, sour cream, etc

## Recipe

1. (quick pickle) Combine [scallions]{ ing="scallions" }, half the [red onion]{ ing="red-onion" }, and [lime juice]{ ing="lime-juice" } in a mason jar. Add a pinch of [kosher salt]{ ing="kosher-salt" }, shake, and let stand for at least 10 minutes
1. Heat [oil]{ ing="extra-virgin-olive-oil" } in a large skillet over medium heat. Add the remaining [red onion]{ ing="red-onion" } and cook without stirring until lightly browned ({~3 min). Add [black beans]{ ing="no-salt-added-black-beans" } and liquid, [chili powder]{ ing="chili-powder" }, [cumin]{ ing="ground-cumin" }, Spanish [paprika]{ ing="spanish-smoked-paprika" }, [Dijon mustard]{ ing="dijon-mustard" }, and 1/4 tsp of [kosher salt]{ ing="kosher-salt" }; stir to incorporate. Cook until the liquid reduces to a thick [sauce]{ ing="hot-sauce" } (~}7 min)
1. In parallel, warm the [tortillas]{ ing="inch-corn-tortillas" }
1. Assemble the tacos with [lettuce]{ ing="chopped-romaine-lettuce" }, [black beans]{ ing="no-salt-added-black-beans" }, pickled [onion]{ ing="red-onion" }, amd other toppings
